  nonce: d8e9  # d8e9
  message: "ANOTHER LAZY-ROW MEMBER, from WI-vafad tranche 3 (2026-10-03, docs/audits/0022 T3-H3): elixir `Task.async_stream` is rowed process_send (\"Task spawns -- erlang:spawn / spawn_link, elixir spelling\"), but it only BUILDS a lazy Stream. The spawns happen when the stream is enumerated (elixir/lib/elixir/lib/task.ex:732-749). Both blind workers proposed NONE. The verifier HELD it because the enumeration call is not rowed, so removing it would leave the crossing represented nowhere: ADR-0049 ruling 4's Lazy shape with no process-side vocabulary value (there is no process_compose). Its siblings Task.async / start / start_link spawn eagerly and stay."  # d8e9
- op: discuss  # cd40
  at: '2026-10-03T19:20:12Z'  # cd40
  by: agent  # cd40
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cd40
  clock: 3  # cd40
  nonce: cd40  # cd40
  message: "WI-tunog sweep done on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/tunog (worktree ~/hg_wt/tunog, from origin/dev fe3c32259d), 6 commits, not pushed. OUTCOME: no row moved. Each named row was read against the library's own source or documentation and tried against ruling 3 with a two-arm fixture run (shipped catalogue vs a counterfactual --io-primitives overlay doing the move; the overlay was never shipped).\n\nNOTE: this item had no discussion entries and no PREMISE AUDIT note when read on 2026-10-03.\n\nPER ROW:\n1. javax|jakarta TypedQuery.getResultStream -- NOT LAZY, a transfer. jakartaee/persistence TypedQuery.java (master 96ebe4ec): \"Execute a SELECT query and return the query result as a typed Stream\"; default body `return getResultList().stream();`. Hibernate 6.6.0 AbstractSelectionQuery: getResultStream -> stream() -> scroll(FORWARD_ONLY) -> doScroll -> resolveQueryPlan().performScroll. Stays db_read. ADR-0049 ruling 4 / measurement 0009 had it under LAZY; the ADR is corrected, 0009 is left as the record of its run.\n2. javax|jakarta EntityManager.getReference -- deferred (\"whose state may be lazily fetched\"; \"create an association to an entity without loading its state\"). HELD: the read is at the application's own entity accessor. Fixture: `w.write(em.getReference(Order.class, id).getNote())` violated with getReference the only source; counterfactual: that flow gone, the getResultStream control flow untouched. Association-only shape is a KIND-MISDECLARED source: residual WI-fazif-pihun-falus-lajaj-fagoj-ligig-tubis-vosas (with a text read of keycloak's 29 production sites: 15 association, 9 return, 3 state read in scope, 2 unclassified).\n3. sqlite3.Connection.iterdump -- deferred (Modules/_sqlite/connection.c returns sqlite3.dump._iterdump(...), a generator on 3.10 and 3.13). HELD: no evaluation site for a non-Django iterable; corpus uses iterate in place (5 of 5, ceph + nova). Fixture `for line in con.iterdump(): f.write(line)`: violated (iterdump only source) -> confirmed_with_caveats, no flow. Note: the `con = sqlite3.connect(...)` spelling does not reach the row at all (no return signature for sqlite3.connect; WI-jidij's territory).\n4. std::net::TcpListener.incoming -- deferred (tcp.rs: `Incoming { listener: self }`; next() = accept()). HELD: TcpStream.read* rowed but unreached because the loop variable is typed TcpStream not io::Result<TcpStream>, so stream.unwrap() is untyped. Fixture: violated (incoming only source) -> flow gone under the move. Residual WI-fokup-fobam-hapis-nuhod-tadim-hudaf-rikid-fumuj.\n5. objc NSURLSession dataTaskWithURL:*/downloadTask* (7 net_recv rows), swift URLSession.downloadTask -- deferred twice (Apple docs: tasks start suspended until resume(); response delivered to the completion handler or delegate). HELD for a different reason: no disclosure value fits (net_listen = bind/accept, server side) and no arrival is represented. AFNetworking A/B: net_recv 2 -> 0, net_listen 0 -> 2, total_io_edges 27 -> 25, all 7 claims inconclusive with 0 evidence in both arms. Residual WI-mapim-pujis-vavav-tujub-sahol-sivit-sagap-kumik.\n6. Ecto.Repo.stream (elixir overlay) -- deferred (\"Returns a lazy enumerable\", ecto master 94d69279). HELD: enumeration is in Enum/Stream. Also found the whole Ecto.Repo row family UNREACHED via `use Ecto.Repo` modules: WI-gabuv-duhob-juvuv-ribaf-jukid-sapus-dimar-zivuj (P2).\n\nWHAT CHANGED: row notes only (java.yaml, python.yaml, rust.yaml, objc.yaml, swift.yaml, elixir-web-and-db.yaml) with citation + reason; new packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_lazy_row_parity.py (15 tests: catalogue pins + the end-to-end shipped/counterfactual pair for getReference, iterdump, incoming); ADR-0049 ruling 4 example list + correction, and the implementation-state paragraph. No boundary changed, so no 0003-method delta was owed and none was run.\n\nTESTS: smart-test (329 affected files) 10163 passed, 1 failed -- tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py::TestFilterNewLines::test_output_never_exceeds_input, a Hypothesis too_slow health check (input generation 1.33 s on a loaded box), not touched by this branch. Mutation control: with every held row moved in the catalogue, all 15 new tests red; restored.\nRerun on the committed tree (test_lazy_row_parity.py + the failing transcript test file): 66 passed, 0 failed. Commits: a83a9b6b37 733e35a1c9 4160e5c961 d005ba9aae 0b4c9c82e7 56f83bc0a5 "  # cd40
