- op: discuss  # 21ee
  at: '2026-10-03T21:18:59Z'  # 21ee
  by: agent  # 21ee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 21ee
  clock: 5  # 21ee
  nonce: 21ee  # 21ee
  message: "Merged in PR #1433 (dev c942a68edc).\n\nAddresses WI-tunog. The sweep is complete and no row moved; each row was judged on its own evidence (branch jgstern-agent/fix/tunog, 6 commits).\n- getResultStream is a transfer: the spec's default is `getResultList().stream()`, and Hibernate executes it through `scroll`. It was never a Lazy member, and ADR-0049 is corrected.\n- getReference, iterdump and TcpListener.incoming are deferred crossings. Each has a fixture whose only source for an in-scope read is the row, and the same fixture with the row moved to db_compose/net_listen loses the flow. That is the WI-lunav repeat ruling 3 forbids. Commands: `hypergumbo verify-claims <fixture> --claims <c> --format json`, with and without `--io-primitives <counterfactual>.yaml`. Results: iterdump violated → confirmed_with_caveats; incoming and getReference lose their function's flow. `test_lazy_row_parity.py` pins both arms, and all 15 tests went red under the move-mutation.\n- The NSURLSession/URLSession task rows have no fitting disclosure value (net_listen is the server side). On AFNetworking the move changes no verdict (7/7 inconclusive in both arms) and relabels 2 net_recv chains as net_listen.\n- Ecto.Repo.stream's enumeration runs in Enum/Stream.\n- Residuals: WI-fazif (getReference association shape), WI-fokup (rust yielded-connection typing), WI-mapim (client-side disclosure value), WI-gabuv (Ecto.Repo rows unreached via `use Ecto.Repo`).\n\nThe general claim that no Lazy row outside Django can move is NOT asserted; this closes on the five named families."  # 21ee
